      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1359395957,
      "text": "Bauhinia petersiana, the Kalahari white bauhinia, is a species of shrubs in the family Fabaceae and the subfamily Cercidoideae found in Angola, Botswana, Democratic Republic of Congo, Lesotho, Mozambique, Namibia, South Africa, Tanzania, Zambia and Zimbabwe. The species is 2 metres in height. The flower is up to 15 cm (5.9 in) wide, with five narrow white petals."
    }
